1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:05,230
Sui, does that mean you were confessed to?

2
00:00:05,230 --> 00:00:09,020
With the intent of marriage?

3
00:00:09,020 --> 00:00:11,150
I think so.

4
00:00:11,150 --> 00:00:14,300
He's once divorced already, but...

5
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:20,180
<i>You've never wanted a child yourself?</i>

6
00:00:20,180 --> 00:00:24,730
<i>Although my older brother
took up the family mantle,</i>

7
00:00:24,730 --> 00:00:29,920
<i>he was always pressured to have an heir.</i>

8
00:00:31,230 --> 00:00:33,430
<i>As a result,</i>

9
00:00:34,820 --> 00:00:38,570
<i>I decided I wanted no children in my life.</i>

10
00:00:38,570 --> 00:00:43,380
Which is partially why I think he chose me.

11
00:00:45,570 --> 00:00:47,720
And you're okay with this?

12
00:00:51,040 --> 00:00:55,550
I don't think I'll meet
an individual like him again.

13
00:00:55,550 --> 00:01:02,700
Someone who choses me,
while knowing my circumstances.

14
00:01:05,220 --> 00:01:07,560
I see.

15
00:01:07,560 --> 00:01:11,580
Then you think he's good for you, too?

16
00:01:14,050 --> 00:01:18,660
I'm definitely considering his offer.

17
00:01:21,010 --> 00:01:23,900
I've watched what you've gone through.

18
00:01:23,900 --> 00:01:26,860
So, I want you to become happy, okay?

19
00:01:28,790 --> 00:01:30,580
Thanks.

20
00:01:44,550 --> 00:01:48,820
<i>Say, did your sister tell you her secret?</i>

21
00:01:50,920 --> 00:01:54,060
Her secret?

22
00:01:57,170 --> 00:02:00,520
I heard your due date is coming up.

23
00:02:00,520 --> 00:02:05,390
They'll be Sui's niece or nephew, right?

24
00:02:07,380 --> 00:02:11,090
I'm sorry, who are you?

25
00:02:11,090 --> 00:02:13,350
How do you know my sister?

26
00:02:13,350 --> 00:02:14,710
And what secret?

27
00:02:14,710 --> 00:02:20,550
Is Sui genuinely excited for your child?

28
00:02:20,550 --> 00:02:22,730
She couldn't be.

29
00:02:22,730 --> 00:02:27,690
She must be so jealous you're pregnant.

30
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:30,460
Excuse me?

31
00:02:30,460 --> 00:02:33,150
What are you...

32
00:02:33,150 --> 00:02:36,250
You're the one who wanted to hear her secret.

33
00:02:37,520 --> 00:02:39,000
Huh?

34
00:02:40,620 --> 00:02:45,710
Sui is infertile.

35
00:02:48,880 --> 00:02:52,480
That's why Himukai
broke off their engagement.

36
00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:56,730
She won't ever attain a happiness like yours.

37
00:02:56,730 --> 00:02:59,430
I truly feel sorry for her.

38
00:03:13,480 --> 00:03:15,320
Sui is...

39
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:18,920
Infertile?

40
00:03:20,270 --> 00:03:25,030
<i>Let's make sure our kids
become best friends, okay?</i>

41
00:03:25,030 --> 00:03:27,640
<i>Are you not interested in having kids?</i>

42
00:03:27,640 --> 00:03:31,600
<i>Sui, I'm always here for you, okay?</i>

43
00:03:32,320 --> 00:03:37,220
<i>Promise me you'll take your marriage
and future kids seriously.</i>

44
00:03:40,540 --> 00:03:42,890
"On her side"?

45
00:03:47,150 --> 00:03:49,320
I'm the worst.

46
00:04:55,030 --> 00:04:57,960
I'm the worst.

47
00:04:59,460 --> 00:05:02,170
I hurt Mizuno, and now...

48
00:05:05,710 --> 00:05:09,250
I never had any right to love someone.

49
00:05:19,190 --> 00:05:20,720
Here.

50
00:05:22,550 --> 00:05:25,660
That's enough moping
and drowning in alcohol for you.

51
00:05:32,930 --> 00:05:36,980
Mao. What're you gonna do about Sui?

52
00:05:41,220 --> 00:05:43,800
You love her, don't you?

53
00:05:49,210 --> 00:05:52,000
You can't trick me.

54
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:54,830
How long do you think I've known you?

55
00:06:01,750 --> 00:06:04,080
Actually...

56
00:06:04,080 --> 00:06:05,770
I think right now,

57
00:06:06,630 --> 00:06:10,730
I need to focus on reorienting myself.

58
00:06:13,140 --> 00:06:18,830
I have to be more honest with myself.

59
00:06:18,830 --> 00:06:21,820
Honest with yourself, huh?

60
00:06:23,330 --> 00:06:25,360
Well, that's not half bad either.

61
00:06:26,710 --> 00:06:29,110
Whatever you do, don't regret it, okay?

62
00:06:34,890 --> 00:06:37,250
A design contest?

63
00:06:37,250 --> 00:06:40,000
Yeah. I want to do this, now.

64
00:06:40,960 --> 00:06:43,130
Where'd your motivation come from?

65
00:06:43,130 --> 00:06:46,550
Our team is especially busy now,

66
00:06:46,550 --> 00:06:49,180
so this is a real inopportune time...

67
00:06:49,180 --> 00:06:52,740
This is more for my sake,
so I'll handle the details myself.

68
00:06:53,630 --> 00:06:55,620
If you're asking why now, well...

69
00:06:57,030 --> 00:07:02,120
Let's just say I want to put in
the effort, for once.

70
00:07:04,030 --> 00:07:07,990
A winning design
would certainly help your career, sure.

71
00:07:07,990 --> 00:07:12,130
But don't major firms
usually win this contest?

72
00:07:12,130 --> 00:07:13,770
Yeah.

73
00:07:13,770 --> 00:07:20,410
But the town they're asking for
aligns with the design of my dreams.

74
00:07:20,410 --> 00:07:22,640
I know it won't stand a chance now.

75
00:07:22,640 --> 00:07:25,380
But one day, I will build something like this.

76
00:07:25,380 --> 00:07:29,730
Which is why I want to take action, now.

77
00:07:32,660 --> 00:07:35,980
I only wanted to tell you all
I'd be participating.

78
00:07:35,980 --> 00:07:39,800
I won't cause you all extra trouble.

79
00:07:42,550 --> 00:07:46,040
"Extra trouble"...

80
00:07:47,800 --> 00:07:51,830
Personally, I'd want you to rely on me.

81
00:07:51,830 --> 00:07:53,270
Huh?

82
00:07:54,180 --> 00:07:55,670
Challenging yourself

83
00:07:55,670 --> 00:08:00,830
is far more important than the end result.

84
00:08:00,830 --> 00:08:02,630
So, I want to help you in that endeavor.

85
00:08:05,020 --> 00:08:08,220
She's right. Don't count us out.

86
00:08:08,220 --> 00:08:11,470
Exactly. You wouldn't be troubling us.

87
00:08:11,470 --> 00:08:15,250
You all helped me when I first arrived.

88
00:08:15,250 --> 00:08:17,350
It's the least I can do to help.

89
00:08:19,090 --> 00:08:20,670
Let's all help Mao, together.

90
00:08:20,670 --> 00:08:22,100
Right?

91
00:08:23,350 --> 00:08:26,850
Don't know how I can help,

92
00:08:26,850 --> 00:08:28,980
but yeah, I'll do what I can.

93
00:08:28,980 --> 00:08:30,490
So noncommittal.

94
00:08:30,490 --> 00:08:32,490
- So judgemental.
- Me?

95
00:08:32,490 --> 00:08:33,650
How so?

96
00:08:33,650 --> 00:08:34,980
It's in your character.

97
00:08:34,980 --> 00:08:36,990
Wow, rude.

98
00:08:36,990 --> 00:08:39,070
You're judgemental personified.

99
00:08:39,070 --> 00:08:43,890
You have gone too far.

100
00:09:03,980 --> 00:09:06,280
Matsubara.

101
00:09:06,280 --> 00:09:08,010
I'm sorry.

102
00:09:08,010 --> 00:09:10,410
Mizuno and I... we...

103
00:09:10,410 --> 00:09:12,600
She dumped you, didn't she?

104
00:09:12,600 --> 00:09:14,140
Huh?

105
00:09:14,140 --> 00:09:15,660
What?

106
00:09:16,270 --> 00:09:17,990
Wait, seriously?

107
00:09:17,990 --> 00:09:19,920
I was joking.

108
00:09:19,920 --> 00:09:22,740
Yeah. Dead serious.

109
00:09:22,740 --> 00:09:24,800
I see.

110
00:09:24,800 --> 00:09:27,340
So, Nana actually...

111
00:09:29,960 --> 00:09:32,120
Matsubara.

112
00:09:32,120 --> 00:09:33,890
I...

113
00:09:36,910 --> 00:09:40,250
If you dumped her, I would've slugged you.

114
00:09:41,430 --> 00:09:43,850
Guess that explains
your sudden motivation, though.

115
00:09:46,890 --> 00:09:49,240
Yeah. But that's not the only reason.

116
00:09:51,790 --> 00:09:57,090
Good luck to the both of us then?

117
00:10:00,720 --> 00:10:03,680
Yeah. Thanks.

118
00:10:16,300 --> 00:10:19,000
Nana, the water. It's overflowing.

119
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:20,410
Huh?

120
00:10:23,980 --> 00:10:26,450
Sorry, I was spacing out.

121
00:10:26,450 --> 00:10:28,790
Thank you.

122
00:10:36,740 --> 00:10:38,690
Here.

123
00:10:38,690 --> 00:10:40,090
Huh?

124
00:10:40,090 --> 00:10:42,830
You like the chocolates
from this place, right?

125
00:10:42,830 --> 00:10:45,940
Sorry, it's about all I can do to help.

126
00:10:49,840 --> 00:10:51,850
Matsubara.

127
00:10:52,710 --> 00:10:54,420
I love it.

128
00:10:56,500 --> 00:10:58,430
Huh?

129
00:10:58,430 --> 00:11:00,180
These chocolates. I do love them.

130
00:11:03,050 --> 00:11:05,380
Oh.

131
00:11:05,380 --> 00:11:06,740
The chocolates.

132
00:11:06,740 --> 00:11:09,060
Thanks.

133
00:11:25,420 --> 00:11:28,360
What are you doing now?

134
00:11:28,360 --> 00:11:30,630
I'm drafting up a potential clientele pool.

135
00:11:31,630 --> 00:11:34,150
Is there any way I can help?

136
00:11:34,150 --> 00:11:39,730
I could gather some documents
on additional land plots?

137
00:11:39,730 --> 00:11:42,000
Thanks, that'd really help.

138
00:11:44,710 --> 00:11:47,820
Had you planned to join
this design contest beforehand?

139
00:11:51,190 --> 00:11:53,430
No. But when I think about leaving,

140
00:11:53,430 --> 00:11:56,650
and going independent one day,

141
00:11:57,580 --> 00:12:00,210
I realize taking on these challenges

142
00:12:00,210 --> 00:12:02,920
and having accomplishments will help.

143
00:12:04,100 --> 00:12:05,940
Independent?

144
00:12:06,810 --> 00:12:09,230
I can't rely on Uncle...

145
00:12:09,230 --> 00:12:13,830
I mean, Mr. Hoshina forever.

146
00:12:14,850 --> 00:12:19,250
I want him to know I'll be okay on my own.

147
00:12:21,360 --> 00:12:23,310
I see.

148
00:12:30,700 --> 00:12:32,750
Everything okay?

149
00:12:33,860 --> 00:12:35,690
Yup.

150
00:12:35,690 --> 00:12:38,830
I'll get those documents to you, ASAP.

151
00:12:53,040 --> 00:12:57,540
<i>So, Mao will leave the office one day.</i>

152
00:13:06,670 --> 00:13:09,550
Hello?

153
00:13:09,550 --> 00:13:11,120
Sorry to call out of the blue.

154
00:13:11,120 --> 00:13:14,030
I considered sending a text,

155
00:13:14,030 --> 00:13:16,630
but I wanted to hear your voice.

156
00:13:17,360 --> 00:13:18,950
Huh?

157
00:13:18,950 --> 00:13:21,080
<i>Monou.</i>

158
00:13:21,080 --> 00:13:25,140
<i>Are you free this upcoming Sunday?</i>

159
00:13:26,860 --> 00:13:28,430
I am, yes.

160
00:13:28,430 --> 00:13:34,310
Would you like to join me
for lunch at Ruby-On?

161
00:13:34,310 --> 00:13:35,960
They recently got a fresh shipment

162
00:13:35,960 --> 00:13:39,630
<i>of winter oysters.</i>

163
00:13:39,630 --> 00:13:41,400
I love oysters.

164
00:13:41,400 --> 00:13:43,620
Thank you for the offer.

165
00:13:43,620 --> 00:13:45,950
I look forward to joining you.

166
00:13:45,950 --> 00:13:50,830
If possible,
I'd like to hear your reply as well.

167
00:13:54,360 --> 00:13:55,880
All right.

168
00:13:57,740 --> 00:14:00,410
Then I'll see you Sunday.

169
00:14:23,020 --> 00:14:27,330
You're... Tsukidome?

170
00:14:27,330 --> 00:14:31,440
I apologize for visiting
without an appointment.

171
00:14:31,440 --> 00:14:35,220
The contest run by Noval Inc., huh?

172
00:14:35,220 --> 00:14:38,460
Yes. The one you won
in your second year as an architect.

173
00:14:38,460 --> 00:14:40,900
You did your research.

174
00:14:40,900 --> 00:14:47,120
I should still have my designs around here...

175
00:14:47,120 --> 00:14:49,120
Maybe it's in this drawer.

176
00:14:57,010 --> 00:15:00,780
Found them.
Feel free to use them as reference.

177
00:15:00,780 --> 00:15:03,950
Huh? You wouldn't mind?

178
00:15:04,590 --> 00:15:08,440
You clearly have the passion,
and you're my junior.

179
00:15:08,440 --> 00:15:10,620
It's the least I can do to help.

180
00:15:10,620 --> 00:15:11,870
Thank you.

181
00:15:11,870 --> 00:15:13,640
Good luck with the contest.

182
00:15:13,640 --> 00:15:16,980
I might have other drafts I can lend you...

183
00:15:23,480 --> 00:15:27,350
I'm glad you're there for her, Hirose.

184
00:15:28,600 --> 00:15:30,070
Huh?

185
00:15:31,590 --> 00:15:33,150
I mean...

186
00:15:34,050 --> 00:15:36,250
I'm sorry, that came out of nowhere.

187
00:15:38,130 --> 00:15:41,510
Please make Sui...

188
00:15:42,200 --> 00:15:47,130
Monou, happy.

189
00:15:49,910 --> 00:15:53,670
This really did come out of nowhere.

190
00:15:54,820 --> 00:16:01,400
Monou will always try
to solve her problems on her own.

191
00:16:01,400 --> 00:16:03,680
She's a person with real strength.

192
00:16:04,410 --> 00:16:07,700
But...

193
00:16:07,700 --> 00:16:10,800
She's also gone through a lot of strife.

194
00:16:11,950 --> 00:16:13,710
Even so,

195
00:16:14,660 --> 00:16:19,060
she lives to her fullest, doing all she can.

196
00:16:20,720 --> 00:16:22,370
So...

197
00:16:23,560 --> 00:16:27,820
Please, make her happy.

198
00:16:35,910 --> 00:16:39,050
And you're okay with that?

199
00:16:43,030 --> 00:16:44,520
Yes.

200
00:16:48,220 --> 00:16:50,340
Tsukidome.

201
00:16:51,470 --> 00:16:54,960
There's one thing you're wrong about.

202
00:16:54,960 --> 00:16:56,390
Huh?

203
00:16:58,350 --> 00:17:03,820
Of course, I do wish to make Sui happy.

204
00:17:03,820 --> 00:17:06,410
However...

205
00:17:06,410 --> 00:17:12,890
My feelings alone won't bring her happiness.

206
00:17:12,890 --> 00:17:18,950
How she feels is equally,
if not more important to the equation.

207
00:17:45,820 --> 00:17:48,170
- Welcome back.
- Welcome home.

208
00:18:11,790 --> 00:18:13,720
Welcome.

209
00:18:23,500 --> 00:18:25,780
Ouch...

210
00:18:29,090 --> 00:18:30,980
Someone...

211
00:18:42,150 --> 00:18:46,000
Please... help me...

212
00:18:52,810 --> 00:18:54,000
Thank you.

213
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:55,300
Thank you for always visiting.

214
00:18:55,300 --> 00:18:56,410
Of course.

215
00:18:56,410 --> 00:18:58,380
Enjoy.

216
00:19:00,990 --> 00:19:02,710
I enjoyed lunch today.

217
00:19:02,710 --> 00:19:04,490
I'm glad.

218
00:19:09,740 --> 00:19:11,560
- So...
- So...

219
00:19:11,560 --> 00:19:13,700
Sorry.

220
00:19:13,700 --> 00:19:16,500
Likewise, sorry.

221
00:19:16,500 --> 00:19:18,150
Go ahead.

222
00:19:20,050 --> 00:19:25,270
I wanted to reply to your...

223
00:19:26,770 --> 00:19:27,850
I'm so sorry.

224
00:19:27,850 --> 00:19:30,170
Huh?
[Shinya Ioka]

225
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:34,580
Don't mind me, take it.

226
00:19:34,580 --> 00:19:36,470
Thank you.

227
00:19:37,330 --> 00:19:38,470
Hello?

228
00:19:38,470 --> 00:19:40,170
<i>Sui!</i>

229
00:19:40,170 --> 00:19:41,600
Shinya?

230
00:19:41,600 --> 00:19:45,680
Rin collapsed. She was taken to the hospital.

231
00:19:45,680 --> 00:19:47,120
What?

232
00:19:49,340 --> 00:19:51,120
Rin!

233
00:19:52,270 --> 00:19:53,440
Sui...

234
00:19:53,440 --> 00:19:57,100
Shinya's talking to the doctor now.

235
00:19:59,500 --> 00:20:01,030
Thank god.

236
00:20:01,030 --> 00:20:04,130
You're both safe...

237
00:20:04,130 --> 00:20:06,620
Sui...

238
00:20:06,620 --> 00:20:08,360
Everything will be okay.

239
00:20:08,360 --> 00:20:12,120
Shinya will be back soon.

240
00:20:13,020 --> 00:20:14,860
No, Sui.

241
00:20:17,070 --> 00:20:19,900
I'm so sorry.

242
00:20:23,390 --> 00:20:25,690
I'm getting what I deserve.

243
00:20:27,140 --> 00:20:31,860
I said so much without knowing anything...

244
00:20:32,960 --> 00:20:35,050
What are you talking about?

245
00:20:37,960 --> 00:20:42,120
Sui, your body.

246
00:20:43,360 --> 00:20:45,300
I heard what happened.

247
00:20:47,170 --> 00:20:51,810
Your old coworker told me.

248
00:20:54,170 --> 00:20:56,300
Takizawa...

249
00:21:00,780 --> 00:21:02,840
Rin.

250
00:21:02,840 --> 00:21:05,990
You're not, "getting what you deserve."

251
00:21:05,990 --> 00:21:09,370
Focus on your baby, okay?

252
00:21:13,790 --> 00:21:16,090
Rin.

253
00:21:16,090 --> 00:21:21,680
I can't wait to meet your baby.

254
00:21:21,680 --> 00:21:28,080
I've been so, so excited for this moment.

255
00:21:29,710 --> 00:21:31,530
Really?

256
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:47,200
Ow...

257
00:21:47,200 --> 00:21:50,740
Rin? Rin! Are you okay?

258
00:21:50,740 --> 00:21:52,720
Rin!

259
00:21:55,890 --> 00:21:58,910
Because the baby remains put,

260
00:21:58,910 --> 00:22:01,120
we'll be performing an emergency C-section.

261
00:22:01,120 --> 00:22:02,860
I'll be removing your stomach pad.

262
00:22:02,860 --> 00:22:04,870
Okay.

263
00:22:04,870 --> 00:22:06,750
Hang in there.

264
00:22:08,370 --> 00:22:10,010
Rin.

265
00:22:10,010 --> 00:22:12,670
I promise you'll be okay.

266
00:22:12,670 --> 00:22:14,760
We'll be moving her.

267
00:22:14,760 --> 00:22:17,380
- Ready?
- Yes.

268
00:22:37,030 --> 00:22:39,690
I heard a passerby helped Rin

269
00:22:39,690 --> 00:22:43,160
when she collapsed.

270
00:22:57,010 --> 00:22:58,800
I'll buy you a drink.

271
00:22:58,800 --> 00:23:00,740
Be right back.

272
00:23:28,200 --> 00:23:30,320
Sui?

273
00:23:31,550 --> 00:23:36,100
I need to ask you a question.

274
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:47,610
I decide my own happiness.

275
00:23:47,610 --> 00:23:51,550
You truly are an honest individual.

276
00:23:51,550 --> 00:23:55,190
I want to become happy,

277
00:23:55,190 --> 00:23:57,940
regardless of whether or not I can do it.
